#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""h713-autofocus -- the vendor's autofocus search, rebuilt for Linux.

The stock autofocus is an Android service plus libduRYXtp.so: it puts a
chessboard on the wall, films it with the internal USB camera, measures how
sharp the picture is and walks the focus motor until the measurement stops
growing. This is that procedure without Android and without the vendor binary.
Built from AP1 (sections 2, 3, 6, 7) and AP1b (4, 9, 10, 11); every constant
below names the section it comes from. Four parts, in the order a run uses:

  pattern  a chessboard, generated here, written to /dev/fb0. The framebuffer
           is the console's surface, so `h713-tv ctl off` hands the panel over
           first; that needs no DRM master and so cannot fight h713-tv for one
           (AP1 7, the first of its three routes).
  camera   YUYV 640x480 over MMAP streaming; the even bytes of a buffer are
           the luma plane. The exposure is written before the first frame,
           which is what wakes this camera out of its black-frame state -
           and again during the warm-up until the picture is there, because
           the first run after a boot measured the dark (23.09.2026).
  metric   the vendor's cubed-gradient sum over a window, divided by a divisor
           the first measurement fixes. That divisor is why the thresholds do
           not depend on window or stride: whatever is measured, the first
           reading lands near 5012 (AP1 2.7).
  search   five states -- settle, wait for a quiet picture, coarse hill climb,
           peak confirmation, fine return. The move sizes come from the board
           profile, not from the code (AP1b 10/11).

Without a device: `run --dry-run DIR` replays recorded luma frames through the
real search with a simulated motor, `measure --metric-only FILE` times the
metric on one frame. Neither opens anything under /dev or /sys.

Safety, the four rules of h713-focus for its reasons: motor_limit is read
before and after every move, an edge stops the run, motor_ctrl_no_limit is
never written, a run has a hard mstep cap. The search writes the stock
autofocus commands 1/2, not h713-focus's manual 8/9 (AP1 6).
"""

